# NO trailing slash, and that is the whole point of this line.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only. A SYMLINK named `node_modules` is a
# FILE to git, so it sails straight past that pattern — and borrowing another
# worktree's `node_modules` by symlink is the documented way to work in a fresh
# worktree here, because `pnpm install` in one takes 30+ minutes and times out.
#
# On 2026-09-03 a `git add -A packages` committed three of those links. CI then
# failed EVERY job at `pnpm install`: `packages/config/node_modules` existed as
# a link to a path no runner has, so pnpm's own mkdir hit ENOENT and the whole
# install exited 254. Nothing about the change under review was wrong.
#
# `apps/web/.gitignore` already used the slash-less spelling, which is exactly
# why only `packages/*` was hit.
node_modules
.next/
dist/
.turbo/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# `!.env.example` only rescues that exact filename, so the deploy templates
# (`.env.dokploy.example`, `.env.production.example`) were being ignored —
# they are checklists of variable NAMES with CHANGE_ME placeholders, and
# belong in the repo like every other `.example`. Still ignores real files:
# this only rescues names ending in `.example`.
!.env.*.example
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
.claude/worktrees/
